# FAST GUNS — environment template
# ============================================================================
# OWNER MANDATE: the app now runs with ZERO configuration. Built-in house
# credentials live in src/lib/server-env.ts (OWNER_FALLBACKS) and are used
# whenever a variable is missing/empty — documented as a public-knowledge
# owner decision in SECURITY.md §11.
#
# Everything below is therefore OPTIONAL: set a variable to OVERRIDE the
# built-in (e.g. to restore real secrecy on a deployment). An override that
# fails validation (burned/weak/too short) fails CLOSED — the server refuses
# to serve; it never silently falls back to the built-in.
# ============================================================================

# Front-door passcode — built-in: the house mark "187" (owner decision).
# The gate is friction + abuse control, NOT the root of message secrecy —
# E2EE session keys carry that. This value also seeds the WANTED-board
# content key client-side (PBKDF2-SHA512, 600k iterations). Any OTHER value
# must meet full strength (min 16 chars in production).
# GATE_PASSCODE=187

# Boss key for the reserved DRACH callsign — built-in: "BIGBOSS27" (owner
# decision). Verified server-side in constant time, never stored or logged.
# Any OTHER value must meet full strength (min 16 chars in production).
# DRACH_KEY=BIGBOSS27

# HMAC secret for attestations + capability tokens — built-in: a fixed
# owner-supplied value (public in this repo, see SECURITY.md §11). Override
# with your own random value to restore the anti-impersonation layer:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# FAST_ATTEST_SECRET=""

# OPTIONAL distributed rate-limiting backend (spec §7). When both are set the
# limiter becomes cluster-wide (keys are HMAC digests — raw IPs never leave
# the app) and backend errors fail CLOSED. Leave unset for instance-local
# limiting.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=""
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=""
